From d421eca1f2ec5c428d416cb425a0f5f34544e384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 11:15:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 286: the composition residual - dead at word level, alive at
 context level

Half of the proposal is refuted by the encoder's own definition and half is
sharper than it was pitched, so both halves are recorded rather than only the
surviving one.

fp(w) = norm(LN(FF(mean_c emb(c)))). The pool happens BEFORE the feed-forward.
So for a word, f(whole) = LN(FF(mean_c e_c)) is a function of the character
MULTISET, and mean_c f(c) = mean_c LN(FF(e_c)) is a function of the same
multiset. Their difference is therefore a function of the multiset alone:
"listen" and "silent" produce bit-identical D. The hoped-for behaviour - same
letters in another order make D diverge - is not merely absent, it is
impossible in this architecture. Word-level D is closed for the same reason
277 closed the ink as a search channel, and it is closed by proof rather than
by measurement.

At context level it survives, and for a reason worth stating. ctx_fp(T) =
norm(mean_w fp(w)). Chunking by single words is degenerate - fp is already
unit norm, so mean_w norm(fp_w) is the mean itself, D comes out parallel to it
and cos(Di,Dj) reproduces the plain ctx cosine exactly. Two spans split at the
value are not degenerate: each span carries its own normalisation, so D
depends on how the words are GROUPED and not only on which words they are.
That is order sensitivity at chunk granularity, obtained without positions.

And D subtracts the bulk mean, which is the part 283 identified as the
crowder: context flattens keys to 0.345 against 0.061 for two channels because
every English sentence has much the same character statistics. D is the
high-pass part of the context channel - what is left after the thing that
makes all sentences look alike is removed.

--ctx-channel delta REPLACES the plain cosine edge with cos(Di,Dj) and adds
|D| as a node rank; both keeps the cosine too. Replacement is the arm the
evidence points at: ink-slices was the same idea as an ADDITION and it cost
the dup win, 0.773 down to 0.333, because 4,417 parameters over a thousand
examples cannot afford a sixth channel. "both" is included so that prediction
can be falsified rather than assumed.

The legacy residual_audit does not transfer and should not be read as support.
It measured a trained WordComposer with a position table, where proj_cos ran
0.28 to 0.48 and a real residual existed; arc_enc has no positions at all. And
even there the morphology deltas clustered weakly - ing at 0.403, plural s at
0.075, cross-tag ing/ly at 0.173 - so the axis was thin in the architecture
built for it.

Ranks only throughout, as proposed: |D| enters as a within-example rank and
cos(Di,Dj) as an edge rank, so the mind may ignore either and a fresh tape
re-ranks both. Widths verified for all six flag combinations.

